{"type":"npc","name":"Lyodaemon (Isolation Daemon)","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":245,"temp":0,"max":245,"details":""},"ac":{"value":32,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"cold","exceptions":[]},{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"holy","value":10,"exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","cryan","daemonic"],"details":"Telepathy 100 feet"},"level":{"value":12},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Lyodaemons personify death through loneliness and separation from others, especially the deaths of lone travelers who die of exposure. They take a cruel joy in separating travelers from their group and overwhelming them with fear and despair. Once they've had their fun, the daemon falls upon their victims with a whirl of mercilessly cold wind.</p><p>While encountered most frequently in the wilderness, some lyodaemons prefer other isolated locations, such as abandoned buildings, forgotten mines, and graveyards. Some stories even tell of lyodaemons lurking outside of outhouses on cold winter nights, for that moment of fear when a farmer realizes they'll have to make the trek back to their home under the dark of a new moon.</p><h2>Abaddon is Other People</h2><p>As daemons go, lyodaemons are relatively rare, yet they are some of the daemons most likely to be encountered by mortals. The reason for this is twofold. First, the fear of isolation is both particularly strong and nearly universal. Second, lyodaemons find the company of other daemons distasteful and, once released from Abaddon to stalk the mortal realm, are loath to return to their native plane. It's said the worst punishment one can inflict upon a lyodaemon is to send it back to Abaddon. Indeed, many lyodaemons would prefer to be erased from existence entirely than be forced to spend a moment with others of their kind.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 250/560/1,030 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Intimidation, Occultism, Stealth, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, elongating, energy resistant (cold,vitality), ice, mind, mind shield, mirrored, sensory (darkvision), space, space shield, spells (Divine: @UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.sf2e-spells.JCQxDEB0CFIoveu6]{Falling Icicles}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.4koZzrnMXhhosn0D]{Fear}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.IxhGEKl63R4QBvkj]{Frostbite}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-anachronism.spells.xxWhyl81w3ckslAU]{Howling Blizzard}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-anachronism.spells.HBJPsonQnWcC3qdX]{Mirage}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.VlNcjmYyu95vOUe8]{Translocate}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.R5FHRv7VqyRnxg2t]{Wall of Ice}, @UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.sf2e-spells.FTjpdbJKibOcgZPN]{Winter's Grasp}), strength, throwing, unholy, water, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Dejan Veskovic","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":7},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":5},"int":{"mod":3},"wis":{"mod":6},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"fear sense (varies) 1 mile","mod":23,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":22,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":19,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":25},"intimidation":{"base":24},"occultism":{"base":21},"stealth":{"base":22},"survival":{"base":25}},"traits":{"value":["cold","daemon","fiend","unholy"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"lg"}}},"_id":"hXhEADjr7NE2YMf8","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/lyodaemon.webp","prototypeToke